\f1\b\fs72 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Kernel Debug Kit for macOS - Read Me
\fs70 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 \
Use the Kernel Debug Kit (KDK) to debug kernel-level code, such as kernel extensions you create.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf2 Performing Two-Machine Debugging
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 The KDK supports the debugging of kernel-level code, such as kernel extensions, from a second Mac. \
- The 
\f2\i target
\f0\i0  device is the Mac that runs the code you want to debug.\
- The 
\f2\i host
\f0\i0  device is the Mac that runs the debugger.
\fs46 \

\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 Identify Device Compatibility
\f0\b0\fs46 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 On Apple silicon, perform two-machine debugging using your Mac\'92s built-in Ethernet ports. \
On Intel-based Macs, perform two-machine debugging using your Mac\'92s built-in Ethernet ports, the Ethernet port on the Apple Thunderbolt display, or the Apple Thunderbolt to Gigabit Ethernet adapter. You may also use third-party Thunderbolt Ethernet adapters that support one of the following chipsets:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0    \'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Broadcom C-IV\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Aquantia AQC107/113\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Intel 82574L\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Note:
\f0\i0  You cannot perform two-machine debugging using USB Ethernet adapters or wireless networking on any Mac.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 You must connect the host and target device to the same network, but there are no other restrictions on how the devices connect to that network.
\fs26 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 Configure Apple silicon as a Target Device\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 Use the following steps to configure your Apple silicon as a target device for debugging.
\f1\b\fs36 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\fs28 \cf2 Step 1: Modify the Security Configuration of Your Mac\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b0 \cf2 Modify the security configuration of your system as follows:\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reboot your Mac in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT201314"}}{\fldrslt Recovery Mode}}.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2.	}Launch Terminal and run the following command to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/disabling_and_enabling_system_integrity_protection"}}{\fldrslt disable System Integrity Protection (SIP)}}:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f4 \cf3 csrutil disable
\f0 \cf2 \
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	3.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If prompted to lower your system security to \'93permissive\'94, enter 
\f4 \cf4 y
\f0 \cf2  to accept.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reboot your Mac.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf2 Step 2: Identify the Correct Ethernet Device \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b0 \cf2 Run the 
\f4 \cf3 ifconfig
\f0 \cf2  tool in Terminal to identify which Ethernet device your target device uses to connect to the network. In the following example, 
\f4 \cf3 en1
\f0 \cf2  is the Ethernet device connected to the network.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf3 en0: flags=8963 mtu 1500\uc0\u8232    options=60\u8232    ether 32:00:13:er:19:e0\u8232    media: autoselect \u8232    status: inactive\u8232 en1: flags=8863 mtu 1500\u8232    options=10b\u8232    ether 40:6c:8f:5b:a2:96\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0inet6 fe80::426c:8fff:fe5b:a296%en2 prefixlen 64 scopeid 0x4\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0inet6 2620::1b07:114:426c:8fff:fe5b:a296 prefixlen 64 autoconf\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0inet6 2620::1b07:114:88d6:bbba:7ac9:b0a7 prefixlen 64 autoconf temporary\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0inet 10.128.19.135 netmask 0xfffff800 broadcast 10.128.23.255\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0nd6 options=1\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0media: autoselect (1000baseT )\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0status: active\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf2 Step 3: Set the boot-args\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\i0\b0 \cf2 Run the 
\f4 \cf3 nvram
\f0 \cf2  tool in Terminal to add the following arguments to your target device\'92s 
\f4 \cf4 boot-args
\f0 \cf2  key:\
\pard\tx540\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl3\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4 \cf3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
debug=0x44
\f0 \cf2 \'97Tells the kernel to wait for a debugger to attach to the device, when the kernel receives a non-maskable interrupt (NMI).\
\ls4\ilvl3\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4 \cf3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
kdp_match_name=enX
\f0 \cf2 \'97Set the value of this key to the Ethernet device (en0, en1, etc.) identified in 
\f2\i Step 2: Identify the Correct Ethernet Device
\f0\i0 .\
\ls4\ilvl3\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4 \cf3 wdt=-1
\f0 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\'97Disables watchdog monitoring.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf3 sudo nvram boot-args=\'93debug=0x44 kdp_match_name=en1 wdt=-1\'94\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf2 Step 4: Reboot the Device\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\b0 \cf2 Upon reboot, you may connect to your target device from the host.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

