\f1\b\fs34 \cf2 \
Configure the Host Device\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 Configure your host device to initiate debugging using the following steps:
\f1\b\fs34 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\fs28 \cf2 Step 1: Install Xcode
\f1\i0\fs30 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 Install Xcode. Then install these additional Python packages for kernel debugging:\
  
\f5\fs24 \cf5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 $ xcrun python3 -m pip install --user --ignore-installed macholib\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5  $ xcrun python3 -m pip install --user --ignore-installed future\
\

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf2 Step 2: Install the KDK
\f1\i0\fs30 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 Install this KDK on the host device.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs34 \cf2 Trigger the Target Device to Wait for the Debugger\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 After you configure the target device, it halts and waits for an external debugger to attach in the following situations:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If the target device panics, it automatically halts and waits for an external debugger to attach.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If you {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/kernel/generating_a_non-maskable_interrupt"}}{\fldrslt trigger an NMI}} on the target device, the device halts and waits for an external debugger to attach.
\f1\b\fs34 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
Connect the Debugger to the Target Device\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf2 Run 
\f4 \cf3 lldb
\f0 \cf2  from Terminal and use the 
\f4 \cf3 kdp-remote
\f0 \cf2  command to connect to the target device. That command accepts the hostname or IP address of the target device, and creates a debugger connection to it. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf3 (lldb)kdp-remote 
\f6\i \{name_or_ip_address\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 The 
\f4 \cf3 lldb
\f0 \cf2  tool automatically searches any spotlight-indexed directories and the 
\f4 \cf3 /Library/Developer/KDKs/
\f0 \cf2  directory on the local system for symbol information. If lldb is unable to find a kernel binary automatically, you can specify it on the command line when you launch 
\f4 \cf3 lldb
\f0 \cf2 . For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf3 lldb /Library/Developer/KDKs/<KDK Version>/System/Library/Kernels/kernel\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 Note:
\f0\i0  Apple silicon doesn\'92t support active kernel debugging. You may inspect the current state of the kernel when it is halted due to a panic or NMI. However, you cannot set breakpoints, continue code execution, step into code, step over code, or step out of the current instruction. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs34 \cf2 Finish Up Your Debugging Session\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

